    "summary": "Prior work establishes that player absence causes measurable offensive identity displacement (reorganization) and that a Leave-One-Out (LOO) simulation can track this displacement. It also validates the reproducibility of structural influence. However, previous attempts to predict the *magnitude* of this displacement using LOO simulations have not been robustly supported, and critically, none of the retrieved studies directly link offensive reorganization to changes in points per possession. The current question is novel in attempting this predictive link."
