    "estimand": "The causal effect of a unit change in observed offensive reorganization (adjusted for player-specific expected reorganization from LOO simulation) on the change in team offensive points per possession during player absence spells.",
    "unit": "Player absence spell for a team (n=148 spells). A spell is defined as a contiguous period of games where a specific 'shaper' or 'connector' player is absent.",
    "sample": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs, and 2025-26 regular season and playoffs (partial). All identified player absence spells (n=148) where a 'shaper' or 'connector' player is absent for at least X consecutive games (e.g., 3-5 games to ensure a measurable 'spell' and reorganization period). Players must meet a minimum minutes played threshold when present to be considered for absence analysis.",
    "power": "A priori power analysis will be conducted based on a minimum detectable effect size for changes in points per possession, considering the historical evidence of 'small sample' risks. If power is insufficient for a reasonable effect size, the study will be re-evaluated or expanded with more data (if available).",
    "controls": "A difference-in-differences (DiD) or fixed-effects panel regression approach will be employed. Controls will include: 1. Team fixed effects to account for baseline team offensive ability. 2. Player fixed effects (for the absent player) or player characteristics (e.g., usage, role, talent proxies) to control for the quality of the absent player. 3. Opponent strength controls (e.g., opponent defensive rating). 4. Game context variables (e.g., home/away, back-to-back). 5. Pre-absence team performance (points per possession). 6. Duration of absence spell. 7. Season fixed effects. The independent variable will be the observed offensive identity displacement (D_A) during the absence spell, potentially normalized or residualized by the LOO simulation's predicted D_A for that player's absence.",
    "falsification": "A falsification test will involve analyzing player absences that are known not to be 'shapers' or 'connectors' (e.g., end-of-bench players) to see if similar reorganization effects or impacts on points per possession are observed. We would expect minimal or no effect for these non-shapers. Additionally, a placebo test could involve examining 'reorganization' and 'points per possession' changes during periods where no key player was absent, expecting no significant effects.",
    "multiplicity": "Only one primary hypothesis test will be conducted for the main estimand. No adjustment for multiple comparisons is needed for the primary analysis. Exploratory analyses will be clearly labeled.",
    "decision_rule": "The hypothesis will be supported if the coefficient for 'offensive reorganization (relative to L)' is statistically significant (p < 0.05) and in the expected direction (e.g., greater reorganization predicts a larger change in points per possession, or a specific direction of change, depending on the operationalization), after controlling for confounders. Effect size and practical significance will also be considered.",
    "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, 2025-26 (complete seasons for analysis, partial data only if rigorously handled to avoid lookahead bias)."
  }
}

